:[{"changed_paths":["instrumentation/influxdb-2.4/javaagent/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/influxdb/v2_4/InfluxDbImplInstrumentation.java","instrumentation/influxdb-2.4/javaagent/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/influxdb/v2_4/InfluxDbQueryLifecycleTest.java"],"commit":"5c2840ad78eac99587b21c0e03d9dc8655f71e3e","parent":"91669ba1f1a6e3d1d21297a08823c5269c56c6c5","patch_sha256":"8dedbd1b97c1c121848ac9c191b5ae33187280a5016c4b031a6253abd2bbe3d3","subject":"Fix InfluxDB async completion without a failure consumer","tree":"18b9ca5c9887053437623e2a64dac34dc78de740"}],"cumulative_patch_sha256":"8dedbd1b97c1c121848ac9c191b5ae33187280a5016c4b031a6253abd2bbe3d3","finding_commits":{"review:5580930133":"5c2840ad78eac99587b21c0e03d9dc8655f71e3e"},"parent":"91669ba1f1a6e3d1d21297a08823c5269c56c6c5","patch_sha256":"8dedbd1b97c1c121848ac9c191b5ae33187280a5016c4b031a6253abd2bbe3d3","tree":"18b9ca5c9887053437623e2a64dac34dc78de740"},"dispositions":{"findings":[{"analysis":"The 2.14 client enqueues query(Query, Consumer, Consumer) even when its failure consumer is null. Async detection now also recognizes the success Consumer at argument 1, leaving completion to the existing response advice. Delayed-response regressions verify statement errors, successful responses, and success-callback failures without a failure consumer, including span and duration-metric assertions. The complete lifecycle suite passes against 2.14 and 2.25, and the 2.4 response compatibility case passes.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"review:5580930133"}],"input_identity":{},"outcome":"fixes","proposal":{"body":"<!--\nCHANGELOG.md is generated from merged pull requests. Do not add an entry unless this PR introduces\na deprecation or breaking change.\n-->\n\nSplits the InfluxDB changes from #20685, correcting query outcomes and duration timing without changing other integrations.\n\n- **Error classification:** Classify HTTP-200 top-level and per-statement errors with bounded `error.type`, never raw error text. Retain available HTTP error codes.\n- **Terminal completion:** End asynchronous and chunked operations exactly once after callbacks and chunk processing finish, retaining callback, transport, and decoding failures, including newer-client decoding failures without a failure consumer.\n- **Cancellation and compatibility:** Make the call available before failure consumers run so pre-response cancellation remains successful. Preserve `DONE` handling, callback parent context, and supported 2.4 APIs.\n- **Regression coverage:** Cover synchronous response errors, asynchronous statement errors with and without a failure consumer, successful and failed chunked completion, cancellation before and after response delivery, callback failures after cancellation, and a single 2.4 statement-error case, with span and duration-metric assertions. Retain HTTP `400` assertions in the existing failing-query integration test.","title":"Fix InfluxDB query error classification and async completion"},"request_digest":"f55987d2dab13cd6d9e9ef539366656fbe49b00c78092f24d41214d0a140120d","schema":2},"download_sha256":"4cc43bd9dc9a9f6c5bbeb49a62bcc7eef9b2aea1e07f67abe33ccdddbdb276d7","frozen_sha":"91669ba1f1a6e3d1d21297a08823c5269c56c6c5","pr":20703,"publication_eligible":false,"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","request_digest":"f55987d2dab13cd6d9e9ef539366656fbe49b00c78092f24d41214d0a140120d","request_id":"8a303e536ff24a63b84e43f7e1553195","run_attempt":1,"run_id":39373120161,"schema":2,"scope":"Structural/Git verification only. No target code or tests are executed.","server_artifact_digest":"sha256:4cc43bd9dc9a9f6c5bbeb49a62bcc7eef9b2aea1e07f67abe33ccdddbdb276d7","verification":"verified","verification_run":{"attempt":1,"id":39375567018},"workflow_revision":"702f9d0316fccd229b4e90e9a01723d297e91b81"},"request":{"authorized_actor_id":218610,"baseline_review_ids":[5566618546,5566651972,5566713561,5577451717,5578038543,5578376761,5580015794,5580024701,5580039812,5580084717,5580599974,5580641996,5580930133],"budgets":{"max_iterations":5,"propagation_seconds":120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udd35 Needs a closer look\n\nAn unresolved asynchronous-completion defect and cross-version cancellation behavior require correction and final human review.\n\n**No open issues** \ud83c\udf89\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>1 previously missed issue</strong></summary>\n\nIn code that hasn't changed since last review\n\n<details>\n<summary><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> Handle async query overloads with a null failure consumer</summary>\n\n`instrumentation/\u200binfluxdb-2.4/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bsrc/\u200bmain/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200binfluxdb/\u200bv2_4/\u200bInfluxDbImplInstrumentation.java:110`\n\n[Javaagent] `query(query, successConsumer, null)` is misclassified as synchronous because argument 2 is the failure consumer. In the tested 2.14 client, this overload still enqueues the request and delivers successful responses to argument 1. Method-exit advice therefore ends the span and duration before the response arrives, preventing later statement errors or success-callback failures from updating them. Recognize the success consumer at argument 1 as well, and add a delayed-response regression with a null failure consumer.\n</details>\n</details>\n\n<sub>Review 